25:["$","div","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Google Workspace and Microsoft 365"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Microsoft 365 (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, OneDrive, and Teams) and Google Workspace do the same jobs. Many offices use one; plenty use both, for example Google Workspace for daily work and Word for a letter that must match a printed letterhead. If you already know a Microsoft app, most of what you know carries over."}],["$","figure","1",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Google Workspace"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Microsoft 365"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Drive"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"OneDrive (and SharePoint for team files)"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Docs"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Word"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Sheets"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Excel"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Slides"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"PowerPoint"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Gmail and Google Calendar"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Outlook"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Meet and Google Chat"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Microsoft Teams"}]]}],["$","tr","6",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Google Forms"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Microsoft Forms"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Which app does the same job"}]]}],["$","$L34","2",{"src":"/images/google-workspace/module-1/what-is-google-workspace/google-and-microsoft.png","alt":"Quick reference: Google Workspace apps and their Microsoft 365 matches, and the differences that matter at work","caption":"Quick reference you can keep: Google and Microsoft apps side by side."}],"$L35"]}]]}]
26:["$","div","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Three habits of cloud apps"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","ol","0",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Changes save on their own. Docs, Sheets, and Slides save every change to Google Drive as you type. There is no Save button. Version history keeps earlier versions in case you need to go back."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"You share a link, not an attachment. Instead of emailing a copy, you share the file, and everyone works in the same one at the same time. You decide who can view, comment, or edit."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Your files open on any computer. Sign in on any computer with a web browser and your files are there. That is also why you must sign out on a shared computer."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-primary-200 bg-primary-50/50 p-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-700 mb-2","children":"Worked example"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1","children":"Why Denise never emails the maintenance log"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Three people update the maintenance request log during the day."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":1}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Keep one Google Sheet in the shared Maintenance folder in Drive."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"If each person emailed copies back and forth, nobody would know which copy is current."}]]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":2}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Share the sheet with Kim and Marcus as editors."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"Sharing gives people access to the one real file instead of making new copies."}]]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Let everyone type into it at the same time."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"Sheets saves every change for everyone, so the log is always up to date."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-primary-200 text-gray-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Result: "}],"One current log that the whole team can see and update from any computer."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-gray-900 font-medium","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"🔑 "}],"In Google Workspace, keep one file and share it. Copies are for people outside the team who need a finished version."]}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"Some Google accounts include Gemini, Google's AI assistant, which shows up as an Ask Gemini button in apps such as Docs. It needs an eligible Google Workspace or Google AI plan, and many employers turn it off or limit it. Nothing in this course requires it. If your job lets you use it, read and check everything it writes before you share it."]}]]}]]}]
27:["$","div","5",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Knowledge Check"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","$L36","0",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Denise asks you to track tenant maintenance requests so three coworkers can update the list during the day. Which app fits best?","options":["Google Docs","Google Sheets","Google Slides","Google Meet"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"A list with columns (date, apartment, problem, status) that several people update is a spreadsheet job. Google Sheets keeps one shared, current copy.","optionRationales":["Docs is for letters and notices. A list that needs sorting and filtering belongs in a spreadsheet.","Correct. Sheets is built for lists and logs, and several people can edit it at the same time.","Slides is for presentations, not for a list people update all day.","Meet is for video meetings. It does not store the list."]}}],["$","$L36","1",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"What is true about saving in Google Docs?","options":["Press Ctrl+S every few minutes or you lose your work","Changes are saved to Google Drive automatically as you work","You must download the file to save it","Only the owner's changes are saved"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Docs, Sheets, and Slides save every change to Drive as you work. There is no Save button, and version history keeps earlier versions.","optionRationales":["That is a Word habit. Google's editors save on their own.","Correct. Every change is saved to Drive automatically.","Downloading makes a separate copy. The file in Drive is already saved.","Every editor's changes are saved, and version history shows who changed what."]}}],["$","$L36","2",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Your Parkview account is jlee@parkviewpm.example. Who controls which features it has?","options":["You do","Google support","Parkview's Google Workspace administrator","Anyone you share a file with"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"A work account is managed by the organization. Its administrator can turn features on or off and set sharing rules.","optionRationales":["You control a personal account. A work account is managed by your organization.","Google provides the apps, but your organization's admin manages the account settings.","Correct. The admin manages work accounts, including sharing rules and features.","Sharing a file never gives someone control of your account."]}}]]}]]}]
